  "summary": "This study used large, manually delaminated Ti3C2Tx flakes prepared by HCl/LiF etching, then made free-standing films by vacuum filtration. Seven electrode materials with electrochemical use are identified: compact pure MXene, uncalcined nanoporous P-MX1.5, and five calcined modified nanoporous MP-MXx films differing in Fe(OH)3-template mass ratio. MP-MX1.5 is the headline and best volumetric performer, delivering 1142 F cm\u22123 at 0.5 A g\u22121 and 828 F cm\u22123 at 20 A g\u22121; it also retained 749 F cm\u22123 at 11.2 mg cm\u22122. The paper does not provide individual thicknesses, pore diameters, porosity, or complete numerical volumetric capacitances for every variant."
